The original three-phase pipeline is retained and reinforced with one non-negotiable addition:

The Unified Cyber-Physical Mandate:
Phase 1 (Foundation) must not permit specialization that isolates structural materials science from embedded AI systems. A logic bug in the prognostic algorithm, a calibration drift in a fiber-optic sensor, and a physical fatigue crack in a load-bearing wall are the same category of threat. Every Phase 1 module must be co-taught across disciplines. The practitioner who graduates must be unable to look at a structural drawing without simultaneously visualizing the sensor embedding plan and the computational failure cascade model.

Phase 2 (Analog Deployment) is unchanged in structure, but the “live inside your own design” requirement is elevated to include at least one deployment where the practitioner’s autonomous system triggers a real Boundary Declaration event and the practitioner must respond as the human expert in the loop.

