A lunar habitat is not a building with monitoring attached. It is a coupled physical-computational system that must know its own state, predict its own decline, and confess when it does not know — across decades of self-repair that erase and rewrite its physical form. The Autonomous Habitat Architect is the profession that ensures this integrated honesty. The v2.0 hardenings ensure that the honesty survives radiation, resource scarcity, and the slow transformation of the habitat into something its original designers never saw. The most dangerous failure mode remains the confident, plausible, wrong assessment. The v2.0 habitat is designed to make that failure mode structurally impossible.

